  "name": "Phase 3 — Kent passage pilot",
  "description": "TTX pilot scenario: the whole planning layer in one exercise. Blue holds the Kent passage with a sense zone and a polygon engage zone; a surface action group patrols the western approach and a corvette holds the passage as the zone's assigned shooter. Blue commands from the destroyer over a line-of-sight net relayed by the corvette, with the maritime HQ ashore as the alternate (5-minute handover, orders queued). Red sends two corvettes west through the passage, one of them carrying a jammer, while a landing ship lays mines on the eastern approach and a patrol boat runs a barrier patrol behind them. Blue has a mine countermeasures vessel sweeping that approach, an oiler at RV Bravo, an offshore patrol vessel low on fuel on a denial patrol, and a supply ship carrying stores from Refuge Cove that then stages at the anchorage. Fuel is on. Dusk falls about 55 minutes in; a gale raises the sea state to 5 from 02:40 to 03:20. All platforms are generic database classes with no real-world values.",
